&lt;h3&gt;


  FAQs
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. What is churn rate, and why is it important?&lt;/strong&gt; Churn rate is the percentage of customers who stop using your product or service over a specific period of time. It's a key metric for understanding user retention, customer satisfaction, and overall business health. Monitoring churn helps identify areas of friction and opportunities to improve the user experience.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. How do I calculate churn rate?&lt;/strong&gt; To calculate churn rate, use the formula:&lt;br&gt;
 &lt;strong&gt;Churn Rate = (Customers Lost ÷ Customers at Start of Period) × 100&lt;/strong&gt; For example, if you started with 100 customers and lost 7, your churn rate would be 7%. Tracking this monthly or quarterly helps spot trends and take timely action.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. What are the most common reasons users churn from Web3 products?&lt;/strong&gt; Users typically churn due to:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Poor customer support or onboarding experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Misaligned pricing or value perception&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Low engagement or unclear product value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lack of trust in the platform or brand&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Incomplete product-market fit for their needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Understanding these reasons can help teams prioritize improvements in UX, communication, and product direction.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. What should an effective churn survey include?&lt;/strong&gt; A good churn survey should be short, embedded naturally in the cancellation process, and include:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Multiple-choice questions&lt;/strong&gt; to identify top reasons for churn&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Optional open-ended responses&lt;/strong&gt; to collect deeper insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, respectful language that encourages honesty
Avoid long forms or questions that feel intrusive - your goal is to reduce friction and maximize useful feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5. How does Formo help reduce churn for Web3 products?&lt;/strong&gt; Formo allows Web3 teams to:&lt;/p&gt;

