&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Takeaways&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Dapp analytics&lt;/strong&gt; is essential for tracking user behavior, measuring performance, and driving product-led growth in Web3.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Core data types include &lt;strong&gt;user data&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;transaction data&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;smart contract data&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;token metrics&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Real-time dashboards&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;automation&lt;/strong&gt; help teams act quickly and make smarter decisions using onchain insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tracking metrics like &lt;strong&gt;Revenue Per Wallet (RPW)&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;churn rate&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;campaign attribution&lt;/strong&gt; enables better targeting, retention, and ROI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unified analytics platforms like &lt;strong&gt;Formo&lt;/strong&gt; simplify multi-chain data aggregation, making insights accessible to both technical and non-technical teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F9xw5ahrcmr8j89folj9u.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F9xw5ahrcmr8j89folj9u.png" width="800" height="465"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Dapp analytics is the analysis of real-time data from Dapps to understand user behavior in-app&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What Is a Dapp?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A &lt;strong&gt;decentralized application (Dapp)&lt;/strong&gt; is software that runs on a blockchain network, powered by &lt;strong&gt;smart contracts&lt;/strong&gt; and accessed via a frontend interface. Unlike traditional apps, Dapps offer:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Decentralization&lt;/strong&gt;  -  Operates on smart contracts executed by distributed blockchain nodes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Transparency&lt;/strong&gt;  -  All transactions are recorded and publicly verifiable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Security&lt;/strong&gt;  -  Immutable data ensures tamper-proof records.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Tokenization&lt;/strong&gt;  -  Many Dapps issue tokens for utility, governance, and ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fot2u4mgyz2c6frq5jldz.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fot2u4mgyz2c6frq5jldz.png" width="800" height="450"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Example of Dapp Architecture&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Dapps power a wide range of industries - from DeFi platforms like &lt;a href="https://app.uniswap.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Uniswap&lt;/a&gt;, to NFT marketplaces like &lt;a href="https://opensea.io/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;OpenSea&lt;/a&gt;, and Web3 games like &lt;a href="https://axieinfinity.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Axie Infinity&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Farkw9col0tug9lsbgyta.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Farkw9col0tug9lsbgyta.png" width="800" height="448"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Top 3 popular dapps: Uniswap, OpenSea, Axie Infinity&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What Is Dapp Analytics?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dapp analytics&lt;/strong&gt; is the analysis of live product data generated by decentralized applications. This includes tracking wallet interactions, transaction flows, smart contract usage, and token movements - giving teams a complete picture of how users engage with their product.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fxtaxwp6fsrih0hywkouq.gif" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fxtaxwp6fsrih0hywkouq.gif" width="560" height="319"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Wallet Activity I Source: Formo&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Benefits of Dapp Analytics:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;User Insights  -  Identify demographics, behaviors, and high-value users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance Monitoring  -  Track key growth and engagement metrics over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth Opportunities  -  Spot &lt;a href="https://formo.so/blog/5-web3-user-acquisition-tools-to-grow-your-projects" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;user acquisition&lt;/a&gt;, activation, and retention gaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive Analysis  -  Compare key metrics against competitors and industry benchmarks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fraud Detection  -  Catch suspicious bots and irregular farming activity before it causes harm*&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;*&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Dapp Data Types
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here are 4 key Dapp data types for Web3 teams to analyze: &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  1. User Data
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Information related to user identities, wallet balances, transaction histories, and preferences is a gold mine of insights. User data helps you understand your audience and better meet your users’ needs. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Active Users:&lt;/strong&gt; Number of daily, weekly, and monthly active users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Visitors vs Wallets: The number of visitors with crypto wallets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Retention Rates:&lt;/strong&gt; Percentage of users returning to your onchain app over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Demographics:&lt;/strong&gt; Countries, devices, operating systems, and languages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  2. DeFi Data
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Transaction data provides a detailed picture of user activity, preferences, and adoption across DeFi. High transaction velocity and volume are clear signals of strong user engagement.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F52xn8aih1j9doye23et1.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F52xn8aih1j9doye23et1.png" width="800" height="480"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;DeFi data provides a detailed picture of user intent and preferences&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Transaction Volume:&lt;/strong&gt; The total number of transactions over a specific period.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Frequency:&lt;/strong&gt; How often users interact with a DeFi app.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Total Value Locked (TVL):&lt;/strong&gt; The amount of tokens locked in smart contracts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Top Apps and Tokens: DeFi positions and token balances of the user across multiple chains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  3. Smart Contract Data
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Smart contract events reveal what users do onchain. Smart contract data is critical for debugging, optimization, and understanding how users engage with the core features of onchain apps and protocols in web3.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Interactions:&lt;/strong&gt; Frequency of interactions with specific smart contracts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Event Logs:&lt;/strong&gt; Detailed logs of onchain events triggered by smart contracts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Function Calls:&lt;/strong&gt; Specific functions executed within a smart contract.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  4. Token Metrics
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Token metrics include key data points related to a cryptocurrency or token used in decentralized applications. These metrics indicate the financial health and user interest in the token.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Token Holdings:&lt;/strong&gt; Analysis of token ownership among users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Trading Volume:&lt;/strong&gt; Activity in secondary markets involving the Dapp’s tokens.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Price Movements:&lt;/strong&gt; Tracking the value fluctuations of tokens.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  5 Steps to Simplify Dapp Analytics
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Although&lt;a href="https://formo.so/blog/web3-product-analytics-best-practices-and-benefits" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Web3 product analytics&lt;/a&gt; can seem complex, it doesn’t have to be. Here are 5 practical ways to streamline the Dapp analytics process:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  1. Choose a Web3 Data Platform to Get Started
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Data platforms such as Formo help Web3 teams capture and analyze onchain data. You can measure key metrics such as Customer Acquisition Costs (CAC), &lt;a href="https://formo.so/blog/product-engagement-score-definition-metrics-growth-tips" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Product Engagement Score (PES)&lt;/a&gt;, Average Revenue Per User (ARPU), and Customer Lifetime Value (CLV). Dapp analytics tools provide tracking dashboards and unified analytics that help simplify the process of analyzing Dapp data quickly with minimal technical expertise.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fno3izro376i3cr4fxei9.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fno3izro376i3cr4fxei9.png" width="800" height="742"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Overview analytic page I Source: Formo&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  2. Leverage Web3 APIs to Improve Data Coverage and Quality
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Web3 APIs from providers such as Alchemy and QuickNode empower Web3 builders to query blockchain data easily. These APIs simplify the process of pulling complex datasets and integrating them into your analysis workflows, saving you time and resources.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  3. Automate Workflows with Integrations
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Automation is key to reducing the time and effort spent on collecting and reacting to new data. Integration services such as &lt;a href="https://zapier.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Zapier&lt;/a&gt;help automate key workflows, such as real-time notifications, ensuring that you act on data quickly and continuously.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fz4m9svp9v2603bs5a1x5.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fz4m9svp9v2603bs5a1x5.png" width="800" height="400"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Zapier connects apps and lets users create automated workflows to streamline tasks&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  4. Define Key Metrics
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Not all data is created equal. Identify and prioritize key performance indicators (KPIs) that align with your product goals. For example, for user growth, focus on &lt;a href="https://formo.so/blog/mau-vs-wau-vs-dau-why-active-users-matter-in-web3" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;daily active users (DAU)&lt;/a&gt;and retention rates. For financial health, track TVL and revenue.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  5. Turn Data into Insights with Charts and  Dashboards
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Tableau, Grafana, or built-in dashboards from analytics platforms make it easier to present complex data in a simple, easy-to-understand format. Interactive graphs, charts, and heatmaps help identify trends, spot anomalies, and track performance at a glance.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Examples of Dapp Analytics in Action
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Understanding what’s happening inside your dApp is about uncovering user behavior, optimizing conversions, and driving sustainable growth. Below are real-world examples of how Web3 teams use dApp analytics to make impact decisions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  1. User Retention Funnel
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Objective&lt;/strong&gt;: Analyze how users progress through the product journey and identify drop-off points.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scenario&lt;/strong&gt;: A DeFi protocol wants to measure how many users:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect their wallet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make their first token swap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Add liquidity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Return to perform another action within 7 days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Metrics&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wallet connect → First swap → Liquidity added&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1-day, 7-day, and 30-day retention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Funnel conversion rates and drop-off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  2. Campaign Attribution
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Objective&lt;/strong&gt;: Understand which marketing channels drive meaningful user actions such as minting or trading NFTs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scenario&lt;/strong&gt;: An NFT marketplace runs Twitter and Discord campaigns with allowlist links.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Metrics&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clicks → Wallet connect → Mint → First trade&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Campaign UTM tracking mapped to wallet behavior&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;LTV by source (Twitter vs Discord)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  3. Revenue Per Wallet (RPW)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Objective&lt;/strong&gt;: Track and improve how much revenue each wallet generates in a play-to-earn ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scenario&lt;/strong&gt;: A Web3 game wants to compare&lt;a href="https://formo.so/blog/revenue-per-wallet-(rpw)-the-metric-for-web3-monetization" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;RPW&lt;/a&gt; across different user acquisition sources (e.g., guilds, ads, referrals).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Metrics&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;RPW = Total revenue / # of active wallets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;RPW by channel and player cohort&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-game purchases, token inflows/outflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  5. Churn Analysis
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Objective&lt;/strong&gt;: Understand why previously active contributors have stopped participating.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scenario&lt;/strong&gt;: A DAO tool notices a decline in proposal creation and wants to investigate.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Metrics&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Last seen wallet activity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Voting and proposal creation frequency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Traits of churned users (e.g., delegates vs members)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  6. User Segmentation
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Objective&lt;/strong&gt;: Group users into segments based on onchain behavior and offchain attributes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scenario&lt;/strong&gt;: A dApp team wants to identify:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Power users (e.g., whales or repeat users)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;New or dormant wallets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Survey responses from high-value cohorts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Metrics&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Frequency and volume of transactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Token/NFT holdings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Form responses (e.g., demographics, motivations)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  List of Dapp Analytics Tools
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here’s a list of tools tailored (or adaptable) for product teams looking to track engagement, optimize funnels, and improve retention in Web3.&lt;/p&gt;

